# Project Structure Guide

This Android application follows Clean Architecture principles with MVVM pattern using Jetpack Compose. Below is the key structure and architectural components:

## Core Application Structure

The main application entry point is [GoLocalApp.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/GoLocalApp.kt), which initializes the app dependencies and configuration.

### Key Architectural Components:

1. **Navigation**
   - [NavComposeRoute.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/navigation/NavComposeRoute.kt) - Navigation routes
   - [NavigationAction.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/navigation/NavigationAction.kt) - Navigation actions

2. **Dependency Injection**
   - [AppModule.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/di/AppModule.kt) - Main app dependencies
   - [NetworkModule.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/di/NetworkModule.kt) - Network related dependencies

3. **Base Components**
   - [BaseActivity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/model/base/BaseActivity.kt) - Base activity class
   - [BaseViewModel.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/model/base/BaseViewModel.kt) - Base ViewModel class

## Layer Organization

### 1. Data Layer
- Location: `app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/data/`
- Contains repositories, data sources, and mappers
- Remote data handling in `remote/` directory
- Local data handling in `local/` directory

### 2. Domain Layer
- Location: `app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/domain/`
- Contains business logic and use cases
- Validation logic in `validation/` directory

### 3. UI Layer
- Location: `app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ui/`
- Contains Compose UI components and themes
- Common components in `compose/common/`
- Theme configuration in `theme/`

### 4. UX Layer
- Location: `app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ux/`
- Contains screens, view models, and UI state
- Organized by features (container/, main/, startup/)
